{"text":"Whole-outcome correction replacing unclaimed 4cd9b14f for audit55563589/reviewf24d2b56. Builder: one signing, canonical-JSON and identifier module (simplification review 55563589, findings DUP-01, DUP-03, DUP-06, DUP-07, DUP-08, LAYER-02, LAYER-04). canonicalize is defined four times (client/src/canonical.ts:58, log/src/canonical.ts:37, room/src/canonical.ts:41, policy/src/integrity.ts:22 over values.ts:30), signingBytes four times with two shapes (room/src/crypto.ts:135 takes payload bytes; client/src/keys.ts:93, log/src/crypto.ts:94 uses domain-dependent raw hash or canonical bytes, and checkers/src/signing.ts:41 signs canonical envelopes), base64url six times, parseStrict twice with a nesting limit only in room's, and the copies already differ on undefined, reserved keys and depth. These bytes decide whether every signature and hash verifies. Also duplicated: entry and room ID helpers and the act-ID regex (room/src/ids.ts, log/src/entries.ts, ui, cli, log/src/verify.ts with an unbounded seq), ID regexes and role and kind lists in eleven files, the error status and retryable tables (room/src/errors.ts, client/src/errors.ts) with six ad hoc refusal builders, the Artifacts token redaction regex in six source files, the log push limits and refusal codes declared in both git and log, and the git-to-log push wire shapes restated in git (git/src/publisher/log-push.ts:24-33). Required: one runtime-neutral module, in contract or a new zero-dependency package, exporting canonicalize, parseStrict, signingBytes and payloadOf, base64url, keyIdOf and publicKeyOf, the digest helpers, the ID patterns as strings, the role and kind lists, the error tables, a refusal builder, token redaction, the push limits and the push wire types; golden vectors shared by every package before the switch; every package imports it; the copies deleted. Keep log/src/roster.ts's independent authority judgement as it is. Current reconciliation: log/crypto.ts:94-100 and room/crypto.ts:143-150 sign entry-v1 over raw UTF-8 hash bytes; canonicalising the hash adds quotes and breaks history. room/test/workerd/log.test.ts:49-83 already publishes/verifies two prefixes and rejects tampering; missing coverage is comprehensive edge vectors. Preserve historical hashes/signatures and deliberate input-layer differences through named adapters; no requirement to collapse asynchronous/client adapters into synchronous Room code. Log roster judgment remains independent. Historical findings/counts/lines below are dated at93a2552e/a6330262, not fresh current-main assertions. Reconcile with reviewed main 344656705140d9bf6539fe44de889d1e21dd2482 and credit already delivered work. All original functional groups remain owed except explicitly credited prior implementations. Schedule acts enabling jam first, then spikes needed for concrete jam work, then jam and the full67-page Artroom docs in parallel (user7363396b/04da4388). No blanket before-J2/J3/public-deployment or empty-backlog readiness gate is added; no deployment is commissioned.","body":{"conditions":"Comprehensive cross-implementation golden vectors precede switching: raw entry hash/domain tags and canonical envelope bytes, undefined/reserved/duplicate keys, depth/numeric/string edges, base64/key/digest/ID bounds. Retain existing Room-publication independent-verifier/tamper tests and historical fixtures. One runtime-neutral owner implements all original wire bytes/constants, error/refusal/redaction/push tables/types; meaningful import/source checks distinguish explicit input/runtime adapters and intentional reexports. Preserve synchronous Room sealing, admitted inputs and dependency/runtime boundaries. Root gates and independent exact-head checker review.","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8592926f1d4d30e3cf282eadc411dacde51d3ac0 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7a3bbf8f3b7ccc7ba4fd596a6bcfe5756d51a77e","target_head":"344656705140d